  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "Dog fighting is mapped as an analogy for men who are offended by such imagery",
  "description": "The visual of two dogs engaged in a physical altercation (dog_fighting) is used as an analogy to represent men who are offended by the image. The text explicitly states that if a man is offended by this scene, he is labeled as a 'faggot', thereby mapping the visual of dog fighting onto the textual concept of male homosexuality and weakness. This is a form of analogical mapping where the visual material (dog fighting) is projected onto a textual entity (the man's reaction) to imply a stereotype about sexual orientation and masculinity.",
